# ── Chapter 1 fidelity pins: "What Counts as Evidence" ───────────────────────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. The fixture is the subject, so it is loaded rather than
# inlined. Run:
#   nibli-pin --kb new-book-plans/utopia-v2.nibli \
#             book-1/01-what-counts-as-evidence.pins.nibli
#
# One entry per load-bearing sentence in the chapter. Private to the author; the
# reader never sees this file. If a verdict flips, the sentence it guards has
# started lying — fix the prose or the constitution, never the pin.

:expect-pins 12

# 1.2 "Hano injured Ivo. A court judged Hano. Both of those are facts."
? injure(Hano, Ivo).
# => TRUE

? judge(Court, Hano).
# => TRUE

# 1.2 cont. "Hano is also a prisoner — but that is not a fact anyone recorded."
# TRUE, and reached only by derivation; the two refusals below prove the second half.
? prisoner(Hano).
# => TRUE

# 1.3 "You cannot simply declare someone guilty. There is no way to write it."
:refuse reasoning /declared derived-only/
prisoner(Zed).

# 1.4 "Nor can you hand yourself the authority to judge."
:refuse reasoning /declared derived-only/
authority(Pax).

# 1.4 cont. "Either the electorate seated you, or you hold a public office.
#            Those are the only two routes."
? public(Court).
# => TRUE

? authority(Court).
# => TRUE

# 1.5 "Koa documented something about Esa. ... Esa's credibility is untouched."
? capture(Koa, Esa).
# => TRUE

? false(Esa).
# => FALSE

# 1.5 cont. "Nor is Koa marked for having looked."
? false(Koa).
# => FALSE

# 1.6 "The floor of rights is entrenched. ... The list of what counts as
#      evidence is not on that register."
# This pin is DELIBERATELY the uncomfortable one. It is the chapter's closing
# admission, and if it ever flips to TRUE the closing section must be rewritten
# — which would be good news.
? permanent(Art_Floor).
# => TRUE

? permanent(Art_Evidence).
# => FALSE
